1
00:05:21,176 --> 00:05:27,176
The last guy she wants is the only one she needs.

2
00:10:42,352 --> 00:10:48,352
Drive Me Crazy is a romance, comedy, drama film directed by John Schultz.

3
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:09,529
Nicole and Chase live next door to each other but are worlds apart.

4
00:21:24,705 --> 00:21:30,705
However, they plot a scheme to date each other in order to attract the
interest and jealousy of their respective romantic prey.

5
00:26:45,882 --> 00:26:51,882
But in the mist of planning a gala centennial celebration, Nicole and Chase find
that the one they always wanted was closer than they ever thought.

6
00:32:07,058 --> 00:32:13,058
Nicole Maris, played by Melissa Joan Hart.

7
00:37:28,235 --> 00:37:34,235
Chase Hammond, played by Adrian Grenier.

8
00:42:49,411 --> 00:42:55,411
Alicia DeGasario, played by Susan May Pratt.

9
00:48:10,588 --> 00:48:16,588
Ray Neelay, played by Kris Park.

10
00:53:31,764 --> 00:53:37,764
Dulcie, played by Ali Larter.

11
00:58:52,941 --> 00:58:58,941
David Ednasi, played by Mark Webber.

12
01:04:14,117 --> 01:04:20,117
Drive Me Crazy is a 1999 American teen romantic comedy film based on the
novel How I Created My Perfect Prom Date by Todd Strasser.

13
01:09:35,294 --> 01:09:41,294
Originally entitled Next to You, the film's title was changed to Drive Me Crazy after one
of the songs from its soundtrack, "(You Drive Me) Crazy" by Britney Spears.

14
01:14:56,470 --> 01:15:02,470
The film received mixed reviews and grossed $22.6 million worldwide.

15
01:20:17,647 --> 01:20:23,647
The film explores themes of high school, prom, next door neighbor.

16
01:25:38,823 --> 01:25:44,823
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
